INSTALLATION NOTES for EmiBSD/arm64 8.0

What is on the medium
---------------------

The install medium's directory 8.0/arm64/ holds:

	bsd.rd		the installer: the kernel with its ramdisk set in
	bsd.mp		the kernel that is installed, as /bsd
	base80.tar.zst	the base system
	comp80.tar.zst	the compiler's set (the libraries and headers today)
	man80.tar.zst	the manual pages
	game80.tar.zst	the games
	SHA256		the sums of every file above
	INSTALL.arm64	this file

The sets are tar archives compressed with zstd; the installer reads them with
its own zstd. There is one kernel, bsd.mp, for one CPU or many. The medium's
/etc/boot.conf boots /8.0/arm64/bsd.rd.

The tested machine
------------------

This release is tested on QEMU's virt machine with the EDK2 firmware
(edk2-aarch64-code.fd), a Cortex-A72 CPU, 1 GiB of memory or more, a virtio
disk of 3 GiB or more and the medium on a virtio SCSI CD-ROM:

	qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt,acpi=off -cpu cortex-a72 -m 1024M -smp 2 \
	    -drive if=pflash,format=raw,readonly=on,file=edk2-aarch64-code.fd \
	    -drive if=pflash,format=raw,file=vars.fd \
	    -drive if=none,format=raw,file=disk.img,id=hd0 \
	    -device virtio-blk-device,drive=hd0 \
	    -device virtio-scsi-device \
	    -drive if=none,format=raw,media=cdrom,file=install80.iso,id=cd0 \
	    -device scsi-cd,drive=cd0,bootindex=0 \
	    -serial stdio -display none

vars.fd is a writable copy of edk2-arm-vars.fd. The console is the serial
port. Other machines that boot with UEFI may work; none is tested yet.

Installing
----------

Boot the medium: the firmware starts EFI/BOOT/BOOTAA64.EFI from the medium's
El Torito image, and that boots bsd.rd. At the prompt, answer (I)nstall.

The installer asks for the host name, the network (answer "done" to skip it),
the root password, the root disk (sd0 on the machine above) and its layout;
the automatic layout fits a 3 GiB disk.

The sets are installed from local media only, a CD-ROM or a disk: answer cd0
for "Location of sets?" and accept the default path. Choose the sets (all of
them by default) and answer "yes" to "Continue without verification?": the
release's sets are not signed yet, and the installer checks each one against
SHA256 instead.

The boot loader is copied to the disk's EFI partition. At the end, halt,
remove the medium and boot the disk.

After the install
-----------------

The first boot runs /etc/rc to a login prompt. Not there yet in this release:
the compiler itself (rc's re-linking of the libraries and of the kernel fails
without it, and the system runs as installed), the network install, and the
signatures of the sets.
